    "result_text": "The full build succeeds \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`, all tests green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `customerCode` assignment on owner creation (`POST /api/owners`), formatted `<LAST3>-<NNNN>`.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`Owner` model** (`model/Owner.java`) \u2014 added a `customerCode` field mapped to a new `customer_code` column, with getter/setter.\n\n2. **New OfficeFloor function** (`rest/function/owner/AssignCustomerCode.java`) \u2014 computes the code: `LAST3` = upper-cased first three letters of `lastName`, `NNNN` = 4-digit zero-padded value equal to `ownerRepository.findAll().size() + 1` (one more than the current number of owners). It mutates the entity in place via `@Val Owner`.\n\n3. **POST pipeline** (`officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`) \u2014 wired a new `assignCustomerCode` step between `build` and `save`, under `govern: [ transaction ]`.\n\n4. **OpenAPI spec** (`openapi.yml`) \u2014 added a read-only `customerCode` property to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct maps it by name (serialized on `GET`).\n\n5. **DB schema/data** \u2014 added the `customer_code` column to all four `schema.sql` variants (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) and fixed the positional seed inserts in hsqldb/mysql `data.sql` (h2/postgres already name columns).\n\nThe acceptance test's global-sequence expectation holds because the count is taken at assignment time: owner A (SMI) gets `N+1`, then A is persisted, so owner B (JON) counts A and gets `N+2` \u2014 consecutive, as asserted.",
